The problem I see is the lack of a keyboard input device.  The guy that
implemented this bypassed this by having a list of "canned" commands to run. 
RT-11 and TSX-11 could fit on an RK05 image, but RSX or RSTS would be
difficult I should think.  I think there are also some fairly strong
requirements on the size of the emulated PDP-11's RAM that might effectively
limit you to RT-11 (or very old versions of other OS's).

